WHAT CHANGED
- planner.ts: planRecallQueries(texts, options?: { toolTexts? }). No-options path
  unchanged (early return, cap MAX_RECALL_QUERIES=4). When toolTexts is a non-empty
  array, rank up to MAX_TOOL_SINGLE_TERMS=2 extra singles from those texts alone
  (newest-first firstTextIndex/textCount/length/firstSequence), skipping !isKeptTerm,
  already-chosen user singles, and COMMAND_STOPWORDS (bash/sh/zsh/git/bun/bunx/node/
  npm/npx/pnpm/cd/ls/cat/echo/printf/grep/rg/sed/awk/head/tail/tee/true/false/mkdir/
  rm/cp/mv/curl/jq/find/sort/uniq/wc/xargs/timeout/env/export/set/eval/read). Phrases
  still come from user+tool via the existing planPhrases scan. Cap becomes 6 only
  when tool texts were supplied. MAX_SINGLE_TERMS / MAX_PHRASES / isKeptTerm untouched.
- recall-wiring.ts collectFrom: texts = userTexts only; extraTexts reversed newest-first
  as toolTexts. Empty check allows extraTexts-only. collect() still delegates to
  collectFrom. CollectedRecallCandidates unchanged.
- recall-query-planner-tools.ts commandTexts: within each segment, path words emit
  before the leading command name so they win the newest-first tool slots after reverse.

